{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1783019788,"nonce":"uoAE0BAlY4cpb/6TZIq2+J1+Bac=","message":"Follow-up: closed the mixed pin+bounce-pool gap the user spotted. _claim_one_fill_locked (bounce_pool.py) now skips scheduling a fill for a position whose weight is already pinned (mirrors the _profile_is_pinned bypass _stage_forward_weight already used at consume time) instead of wastefully bouncing a copy that consume_without_transfer would just discard. This combination (partial auto-pin + active bounce pool) was previously untested territory: pin coverage was always ~0% or ~100% before today's cap fix, so 'mixed' never happened in runs 1-7. New tests: tests/test_bounce_pool.py::PinnedSourceFillSkipTests (3 tests, one end-to-end against the real worker thread).\n\nAlso surfaced and fixed a live-environment coupling in the fix from the prior comment: _pin_available_headroom() (the floor guard in _move_params_to_cpu_and_pin) reads REAL psutil available RAM unconditionally, un-mocked. Mid-session this machine's available RAM dropped to 5.76 GiB (below the 6 GiB default floor) from all the GPU probe scripts, which silently zeroed pinning in test_pinned_budget_cycle.py and test_pin_quantized_weights.py even though those tests budget/mock everything else. Fixed by having those two test files disable the floor via AI_TOOLKIT_PINNED_WEIGHT_AVAILABLE_FLOOR_GIB=0 in setUp - they test budget/pin-path correctness, not host headroom. Worth remembering: any test that reaches _move_params_to_cpu_and_pin must now either mock this env var or accept it's exercising live-RAM behavior. Full suite: 125 passed.","files":null}]}